  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The Department of the Treasury obligated $277M in FY2027 to date for federal contracts. The Department awarded 336 contracts so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $825K. The Department's current-year obligations are down 96.0% year over year. The Department historically obligated higher totals: FY22 $9.3B, FY23 $10.3B, FY24 $9.3B, FY25 $8.6B, and FY26 $7B. The Department's FY2027 mix is concentrated: Nonferrous Metal (except Aluminum) Smelting and Refining accounts for $144M, while Copper Rolling, Drawing, Extruding, and Alloying accounts for $32.6M. The Department also obligated funds for Other Computer Related Services at $25.7M and Paper Mills at $19.2M. The Department's vendor list reflects that concentration. STONEX FINANCIAL LTD received $144M, CRANE & CO., INC. received $20.4M, and WIELAND ROLLED PRODUCTS NORTH AMERICA, LLC received $17.9M. The Department's totals are partial because current-year figures are fiscal year to date and not full-year amounts.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What drove the drop in Treasury contract obligations?",
        "body": "The Department of the Treasury obligated $277M in FY2027 to date, down 96.0% year over year. The Department's fiscal history shows larger obligations in prior years: FY26 $7B and FY25 $8.6B, which explains the magnitude of the decline when compared to the current fiscal year to date total. The Department's top single sector allocation to Nonferrous Metal at $144M and a small set of large vendor awards concentrated spending in FY2027 to date."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which vendors and industries received Treasury contract dollars in FY2027 to date?",
        "body": "The Department allocated $144M to Nonferrous Metal (except Aluminum) Smelting and Refining and $32.6M to Copper Rolling, Drawing, Extruding, and Alloying. The Department's top vendors are STONEX FINANCIAL LTD at $144M, CRANE & CO., INC. at $20.4M, and WIELAND ROLLED PRODUCTS NORTH AMERICA, LLC at $17.9M. The Department also obligated funds for computing and services categories such as Other Computer Related Services at $25.7M and Software Publishers at $12.7M."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Department of the Treasury spend on contracts?",
      "a": "The Department of the Treasury obligated $277M in contracts in FY2027 to date. The Department issued 336 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $825K, and obligations are down 96.0% year over year."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Treasury buy?",
      "a": "Treasury buys a mix of metals, industrial and technology services, and power generation, led by Nonferrous Metal (except Aluminum) Smelting and Refining at $144M. The Department also obligated $32.6M for Copper Rolling, Drawing, Extruding, and Alloying, $25.7M for Other Computer Related Services, and $19.2M for Paper Mills, among other categories."
    },
    {
      "q": "Who are Treasury's largest contractors?",
      "a": "Treasury's largest contractors in FY2027 to date are STONEX FINANCIAL LTD at $144M, CRANE & CO., INC. at $20.4M, and WIELAND ROLLED PRODUCTS NORTH AMERICA, LLC at $17.9M. The Department also awarded PMX INDUSTRIES, INC. $14.7M and FCN, INC. $9.7M, with additional vendors receiving smaller amounts."
